  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-47066-RE.0554</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK Resettlement Scheme (UKRS) and the Mandate Scheme (MRS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UK Resettlement Scheme (UKRS) supports the resettlement of up to 2,500 vulnerable refugees to the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland (UK). In delivering the UKRS, IOM will work closely with the UK Government to  facilitate accommodation matching support, facilitate the early identification of beneficiaries&apos; physical mental health needs in line with the UK Health Protocol and through the application of the Global Mental Health Assessment Tool (GMHAT), identify children&apos;s Special Educational Needs  (SEN) using targeted SEN questions in the health assessments, establish enhanced travel assistance, including escorts and transit and arrival assistance and provide refugees information on life in the UK through bespoke sessions delivered pre-departure. Working along the resettlement and integration continuum and recognising the need for integration stakeholders such as the Regional Strategic Migration Partnerships (RSMP) and UK Local Authorities to better support refugees arriving through resettlement, IOM will deliver capacity building information sessions on the cultural, social, educational and economic background and experiences of refugees identified as eligible for the UK Resettlement Scheme.</narrative>
  </description>
